🧩 1. Compile your Java code
  If your main class is App.java, compile it: 
    
      App Main.java

This will produce a App.class file (and possibly others).

  
📦 2. Create a manifest file
  You need a file called manifest.txt that tells Java which class to run:

    manifest.txt => Main-Class: Main
⚠️ Note: There must be a newline at the end of this file!


🪄 3. Package into a JAR
  Run this command to create the executable JAR:

    jar cfm app.jar manifest.txt App.class num7/Num.class

  
🚀 4. Run the JAR
  Now you can run your program like this:

    java -jar app.jar
